      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"bypass rational scrutiny\" ... that's exactly what i mean. it's creepy. it's like they've mapped out how to basically hack our lizard brains so we don't even realize we're being manipulated. \n\ndo you think this goes beyond just \"marketing strategy\"? if they're using specific geometric frequencies or certain light spectrums in that blue to actually trigger a physiological response, isn't that more like psychological conditioning than just selling a bag? like, is there actual evidence that these specific patterns are used to override willpower?",
